Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||05-28-2001||09:32 PM||||Anyone done this? i want to paint my mirrors to match my car. Condition wise there mint. I have a good quality gun ,a Compressor ..ect..ect. what should i do to paint them?? I will remove them from the car to do the job, But I need help.<P>Wet sanding<BR>What brand paint?<BR>Reducer <BR>Primer??<P>The mirrors do have a few chips in them from the previous owner , But I'm sure I can sand them out.<P>Just want to do this once . I have touched up the black a million times ,  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||05-28-2001||09:51 PM||||I removed and completely disassembled them. Then just prep them like any other part. The only tricky part is getting the mirror off. You must gently pry or firmly pull the mirror and backing of for the electric mirrors.  I have not done manual mirrors but are probably similar.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||05-28-2001||10:57 PM||||Where is the connector for the electric mirror?? I thought it was in the door panel , whats the procedure in taking them off??<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||05-28-2001||11:22 PM||||Remove the black thing ahead of the door panel and behind the mirror.  Two 10mm nuts hold the mirror on, get them with a open/box end wrench.  The mirror can be disconnected, there should be a plug just a few inches behind the mirror.<P>I just took a look at mine, yes you have to remove the door panel.  I forgot one of the screws that holds the black closeout seal piece is covered by the door panel.  Taking the interior door panel off is too easy than to try to bend it back to get to the screw and risk damaging it.<P>The mirror itself snaps off, kinda tricky.  I removed the motor guts and everything in mine when I painted them.  Make sure to blow some paint on the visible parts of the inside to give them a clean look.<P>Whoo hoo 1000 posts!<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 05-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||05-28-2001||11:24 PM||||I guess I type too slow, Tigger beat me!<P>Congrats on the big 1k man!<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 05-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||05-28-2001||11:33 PM||||Actually, I can help with the paint too if you are going to spray it with a gun.<P>All that you need to do is go down to your local auto paint supply shop and have them mix you up a pint of your cars color.  You may actually want to get a quart of it if you have not sprayed with a gun before.  They will give you all the reducer and hardener you need, along with some instructions on mixing for that particular type of paint (mixing instructions are based on temp, humidity, flash time desired and primer used)<P>Just follow the instructions there and you should get it mixed fine.<P>There are a variety of paint brands you can use.  I do recommend a single stage paint to keep your costs down.  Yes, you can go with bc/cc, but clear these days can run you $50-90 a quart (once you include reducer and hardener).  I have used DuPont Centari single stage paint before and have had no problems with it; it is a quality paint.<P>As for primer, there are plenty of choices for primer.  Just tell the person helping you with your paint what you are doing, and that you'll need just a basic primer for it.<P>Good luck, hope they come out good!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
